<div class="page prose">
  <h1>The original</h1>
  <p>The images on this website are optimized for viewing on a screen. The <em>original</em> is different: a high-resolution file made from the photographic master, suitable for printing — including large-format prints for your wall.</p>
  <h2>What you get</h2>
  <p>A high-quality, full-resolution JPEG of the photograph, without watermarks, delivered digitally. Exact pixel dimensions are listed with each purchase where available.</p>
  <h2>What it costs</h2>
  <p>${{ site.original.price }} {{ site.original.currency }} per FotoDumka. This is a starting price and may change. Some works are deliberately view-only and have no original available — that is an editorial decision, not a technical one.</p>
  <h2>What you may do with it</h2>
  <p>The purchase grants a personal, non-commercial licence: print it, frame it, give a print to a friend, keep it. It does not grant resale, redistribution, sublicensing, or commercial reproduction rights, and it does not transfer copyright. Copyright in every photograph and text remains with the author.</p>
  {% if site.contact_email %}<p>For commercial use of any image, <a href="mailto:{{ site.contact_email }}?subject=Commercial%20licence%20enquiry">write to me</a> — commercial licensing is handled separately and individually.</p>{% else %}<p>Commercial use of any image is handled separately and individually — it is never included in the personal-use original.</p>{% endif %}
  <p class="muted">This page is a plain-language summary, not legal advice.</p>
